WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:05.450
Alright, this is part two of our osmosis lab.

00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:09.692
If your kit came with these things called Orbeez, then you can

00:00:09.742 --> 00:00:11.950
use these instead of gummy bears.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:14.079
Just be really careful with them.

00:00:14.129 --> 00:00:17.950
You don't want little kids to get them, or dogs to get them.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:22.950
So make sure you're really careful, and dispose of them in a proper way.

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:35.950
[Audio unclear]

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:41.350
And then you also have these cups as well.

00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:44.950
So this one's for measuring,

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:49.950
[Audio unclear]

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:52.950
So let's go ahead and take a look at what we did.

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:59.350
Go ahead and take out each of them.

00:00:59.400 --> 00:01:09.850
[Audio unclear]

00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:15.450
Let's go ahead and look at the size changes in the gummy bears.

00:01:15.500 --> 00:01:19.620
So the first one was the water, the second one was the sugar,

00:01:19.670 --> 00:01:20.850
and then the salt.

00:01:20.900 --> 00:01:25.650
And we can visually see the size difference just by looking at them.

00:01:25.700 --> 00:01:30.850
But when you use the measuring tape, remember to use the centimeter side.

00:01:30.900 --> 00:01:37.760
When you do the measuring, go ahead and measure from his head

00:01:37.810 --> 00:01:43.650
to his toes. So for this one, it was 20 millimeters.

00:01:43.700 --> 00:01:50.450
And then when I go to measure the second one, the second one will be

00:01:50.500 --> 00:01:56.087
19 millimeters. And then we can take the average of those, which

00:01:56.137 --> 00:02:01.724
is almost exactly the same. When I go to measure the sugar ones,

00:02:01.774 --> 00:02:03.750
they are 17 millimeters

00:02:03.800 --> 00:02:12.150
and 16 millimeters as well, so I'll average those.

00:02:12.200 --> 00:02:17.367
And then the little smaller ones, they're very, very tiny.

00:02:17.417 --> 00:02:21.145
They are 9 millimeters and 10 millimeters.

00:02:21.195 --> 00:02:24.833
So we can see it's changed there as well.

00:02:24.883 --> 00:02:30.050
Then you'll use that information to make your observations

00:02:30.100 --> 00:02:38.350
and figure out how the water moved, and how this relates to osmosis.
